agent-ops task task-f194de00-37cf-4645-ab86-eca4cd554e8e: Support cross-host takeover on run resume --host <claude|codex>
intent: Allow agent-ops run resume <id> --host <claude|codex> to switch a paused, blocked, or budget-limited run to another supported host when all writers and proof processes are confirmed dead, rebinding state.host and non-delivered workers while preserving delivered workers, resetting nativeInstance, recording RUN_HOST_SWITCHED, and syncing CLI help, managed auto-run rules, and bilingual specifications.
criteria:
- c1-resume-host-takeover: Omitting --host on run resume preserves baseline same-host behavior; supplying --host <claude|codex> (alone or combined with --retry-delivery or --retry-approval) switches a paused, blocked, or budget-limited run before integration only when all writers and proof processes have confirmed non-future death timestamps (rejecting invalid run states, active/unconfirmed/future-dated writers, or active proof processes with RUN_HOST_SWITCH_INVALID, and rejecting unauthorized host modifications outside resume), rebinds the coordinator and non-delivered workers to start clean native sessions on the target host without reusing prior host session identifiers while keeping delivered workers and their deliveries untouched, records a RUN_HOST_SWITCHED audit event, and preserves mandatory verification and two-round review finalization gates.
- c2-cli-and-autorun-surface: CLI argument parsing accepts --host <claude|codex> on run resume and forwards it to the resume service, rejects unsupported host values or --host on non-resume control actions with CLI_INVALID_OPTION, fails preflight with RUN_NATIVE_UNAVAILABLE when the target host CLI binary or version check is unavailable, and includes agent-ops run resume <id> [--host <claude|codex>] in CLI run help text and managed auto-run baseline instructions.
- c3-spec-sync: Bilingual specifications (docs/en/spec/loop-engineering.md, docs/zh-TW/spec/loop-engineering.md, docs/en/spec/harness-adapters.md, docs/zh-TW/spec/harness-adapters.md) accurately and consistently document cross-host run resume takeover, preconditions, worker rebinding, delivered worker preservation, mandatory verification/two-round review gates, and RUN_HOST_SWITCHED auditing.
